<% content_for :header_tags do %>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag 'performance', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey' %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag 'performance_owner_picker', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey', defer: true %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag 'performance_navigation', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey', defer: true %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag 'performance_leaderboard', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey', defer: true %>
<% end %>
<% html_title 'Performance Results — Returns' %>
<div class="performance-page">
  <%= render 'header', page_title: 'Performance Results — Returns' %>
  <p class="performance-context">Selected project and all subprojects · Visible tickets only · Open as of <%= format_date(@date) %>
    <%= performance_tip('Uses the Tickets tracker scope, current-owner attribution and historical status. New, On-Hold and closed statuses are excluded; Ongoing remains in the open population. The primary metric divides incidents by open tickets with at least one return, not all open tickets. All qualifying incidents belong to the current owner, including incidents before reassignment. Counts stop at the selected date.') %></p>
  <% if @returns %>
    <details class="performance-section performance-comparison" open>
      <summary><strong>Developer comparison — <%= @selected_owners.size %> selected owner(s)</strong></summary>
      <p>Counts are tickets in each bucket. Only tickets open at the selected report date enter these actionable distributions. Consecutive counts accumulate repeats of the same source stage across successive qualifying return incidents; intermediate workflow transitions do not reset them.</p>
      <div class="autoscroll"><table class="list performance-return-comparison">
        <colgroup><col class="return-owner-col"><col class="return-open-col"><col span="8" class="return-bucket-col"><col class="return-incidents-col"><col span="2" class="return-ratio-col"></colgroup>
        <thead><tr><th rowspan="2"><%= performance_return_heading('Ticket Owner', 'owner') %></th><th rowspan="2"><%= performance_return_heading('Open Tickets', 'open') %></th><th colspan="5" class="return-count-group">Number of Tickets with:</th><th colspan="3" class="return-repeat-group">Number of Tickets with Consecutive Returns: <%= performance_tip(performance_consecutive_returns_definition) %></th><th rowspan="2" class="return-ratio-group"><%= performance_return_heading('Total Return Incidents', 'incidents') %></th><th rowspan="2" class="return-ratio-end"><%= performance_return_heading('Incidents / Returned Open Tickets', 'ratio') %></th><th rowspan="2"><%= performance_return_heading('Incidents (excl. merge conflicts) / Returned Open Tickets', 'adjusted_ratio') %></th></tr>
          <tr><% ['0 return', '1 return', '2 returns', '3 returns', '3+ returns', '1', '2', '2+'].each_with_index do |label, index| %><th><% if index == 4 || index == 7 %><abbr title="<%= index == 4 ? '4 or more returns' : '3 or more accumulated consecutive returns' %>" tabindex="0"><%= label %></abbr><% else %><%= label %><% end %></th><% end %></tr></thead>
        <tbody><% @return_comparison.each do |entry| %><%= render 'return_comparison_row', report: entry[:report], ids: [entry[:owner].id.to_s], label: entry[:owner].name, total: false %><% end %></tbody>
        <tfoot><%= render 'return_comparison_row', report: @returns, ids: @selected_owner_ids, label: 'Total', total: true %></tfoot>
      </table></div>
    </details>
    <%= render 'leaderboard', entries: @leaderboard_entries if @leaderboard_entries %>
    <%= render 'return_types' %>
    <h3 class="performance-team-heading">Combined Results for selected owners (team)</h3>
    <div class="performance-return-distributions">
      <%= render 'return_distribution', number: 1, title: 'Return Count Distribution (Open Tickets)', keys: %w[returns_0 returns_1 returns_2 returns_3 returns_4], labels: ['0 Return', '1 Return', '2 Returns', '3 Returns', '3+ Returns'], denominator: @returns[:open], total_metric: 'returns_open', total_label: 'Total Open Tickets' %>
      <%= render 'return_distribution', number: 2, title: 'Consecutive Return Distribution (Open Tickets)', keys: %w[repeats_1 repeats_2 repeats_3], labels: ['1 Consecutive Return', '2 Consecutive Returns', '2+ Consecutive Returns'], denominator: @returns[:with_repeats], total_metric: 'repeats_all', total_label: 'Tickets with Consecutive Returns' %>
    </div>
    <section class="performance-section">
      <h3><span class="performance-step">3</span> Return Ticket Metric <%= performance_tip('All return incidents divided by open tickets with at least one return. This is an average incident count per returned ticket, not a percentage. No returned tickets means N/A (not applicable); incident and ticket counts remain 0. Lower is better; no new severity thresholds have been assigned.') %></h3>
      <div class="performance-return-ratios">
        <article class="performance-metric performance-return-metric"><h4>Incidents per Returned Open Ticket</h4><strong class="performance-return-value"><%= performance_number(@returns[:ratio]) %></strong><p><%= performance_return_link(@returns[:incidents], 'return_incidents') %> total return incidents</p><p><%= performance_return_link(@returns[:returned], 'return_incidents') %> open tickets with at least one return</p><p><%= performance_return_metric_note(@returns) %></p><p>Includes Merge Conflict · Lower is better</p></article>
        <%= render 'return_non_merge_metric', report: @returns, title: 'Non-Merge Incidents per Returned Open Ticket', numerator_metric: 'non_merge_incidents', denominator_metric: 'non_merge_denominator', unknown_metric: 'unknown_return_reasons' %>
      </div>
      <p>The former 10%/50% thresholds do not apply to incidents per returned ticket. No replacement thresholds are assumed.</p>
      <%= render 'return_trend', points: @return_trend if @return_trend %>
    </section>
    <%= render 'owner_change_note' %>
    <details class="performance-notes"><summary>Calculation notes</summary>
      <p>Returns are qualifying transitions into explicit Returned, using the existing tracker/stage mappings. Counts stop at the selected date. Lifetime native Return Count may include newer incidents; it is unchanged.</p>
      <p>Feedback, Feedback gives 1 consecutive repeat; Feedback, Feedback, Feedback gives 2; Feedback, Feedback, Review, Review gives 2. Each repeat after the first at the same stage adds one, accumulating across stages without resetting. Tickets with no repeats are excluded only from the consecutive-distribution denominator.</p>
      <p>“3+ Returns” means 4 or more, and “2+ Consecutive Returns” means 3 or more. Merge Conflict remains in both distributions and the total ratio, and is excluded only from the adjusted ratio. No two-week exemption applies. The reason at each incident is reconstructed from field 66 history; missing history falls back to current reason when available. Hidden/missing reasons are not assumed non-merge.</p>
      <p>Totals use distinct tickets and recorded events. The primary metric is N/A when no open tickets have a return; zero incidents and the open population remain visible. The non-Merge metric divides known non-merge incidents by all returned open tickets, including merge-only tickets. A real zero numerator with a nonzero denominator is shown as 0. Missing reasons make that metric unavailable. Rounding may make distribution percentages differ slightly from 100%.</p>
    </details>
  <% else %><p class="nodata">Select Ticket Owner(s) and As of Date, then click Apply. No return report has been calculated yet.</p><% end %>
</div>
